141
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:02,940
The Dragon's Tears

142
00:02:00,650 --> 00:02:02,980
Let's try this again, shall we?

143
00:02:02,980 --> 00:02:05,480
How did the kind of imbecilic gentlemen

144
00:02:05,860 --> 00:02:08,300
who'd rave like idiots 
outside of our establishment

145
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:11,360
come into possession of these VIP tickets?

146
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:13,840
Th-Th-They were gifts!

147
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:15,300
Gifts, you say?

148
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:17,210
You didn't steal them 
or find them on the ground?

149
00:02:17,210 --> 00:02:18,420
Certainly not!

150
00:02:18,420 --> 00:02:19,960
We took them from our friend's roomâ

151
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:21,170
Our friend let us have them!

152
00:02:21,170 --> 00:02:22,700
Our good friend Cid!

153
00:02:23,090 --> 00:02:24,420
It's true! Good ol' Cid!

154
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:27,750
He told us to take 'em and ask 
the ladies of Mitsugoshi out on a date!

155
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:31,420
This Cid...

156
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:33,430
Are you referring to 
the Young Master Cid Kagenou?

157
00:02:33,430 --> 00:02:34,750
Yes, that's the guy!

158
00:02:34,750 --> 00:02:37,210
My bosom buddy, Cid Kagenou!

159
00:02:37,210 --> 00:02:38,420
I see...

160
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:41,680
By the way, Miss, do you happen 
to be acquainted with our friend Cid?

161
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:43,600
In that case, today can be the day 
you get acquainted withâ

162
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:45,100
Shut up! That's enough!

163
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:49,250
He took the tickets we arranged for him 
and gave them to his classmates,

164
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:48,500
Maybe it was a bad idea 
to take them without asking.

165
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:51,110
Don't look at me! It was your idea!

166
00:02:49,250 --> 00:02:51,110
thus calling the Numbers to assemble.

167
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:54,540
I assume Master Cid Kagenou 
will be present on this date?

168
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:56,380
O-O-Of course he will!

169
00:02:56,380 --> 00:02:57,710
H-He'll be there! I swear!

170
00:02:57,710 --> 00:02:59,690
I know in my heart that he will!

171
00:02:59,690 --> 00:03:04,750
<i>I never imagined he would use students 
from the Academy like this to send such a complicated code.</i>

172
00:03:04,750 --> 00:03:07,390
<i>What does Lord Shadow truly want from us?</i><i></i>

173
00:03:07,880 --> 00:03:09,880
<i>I'll have to seek counsel 
from the Seven Shades.</i><i></i>

174
00:03:11,710 --> 00:03:12,880
Um, Miss?

175
00:03:13,170 --> 00:03:14,840
What is your answer?

176
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:17,000
About our d-d-date...

177
00:03:18,710 --> 00:03:20,710
It is a very appealing offer.

178
00:03:21,380 --> 00:03:23,980
I will take it into serious 
consideration as an option.

179
00:03:24,510 --> 00:03:27,270
So, quit running your mouths off 
and sit still, you little brats!

180
00:03:32,460 --> 00:03:33,570
I understand.

181
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:38,780
He gave his tickets to his classmates 
and invited Shadow Garden's Numbers.

182
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:42,800
Then, with some purpose in mind, 
use the tactic of a "group date" to invite meâ

183
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:46,370
To invite us to join him 
at Mitsugoshi Hot Springs Land.

184
00:03:48,540 --> 00:03:51,710
If I may ask, 
what is Mitsugoshi Hot Springs Land?

185
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:52,800
Eta?

186
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:54,130
Yeah?

187
00:03:54,130 --> 00:03:56,200
You designed the resort, no?

188
00:03:57,230 --> 00:04:02,710
Mitsugoshi Hot Springs Land is a relaxation resort complex 
set to open this coming week.

189
00:04:02,710 --> 00:04:05,340
With the theme based on the legend 
of the Dragon's Tears, this groundbreakingâ

190
00:04:05,340 --> 00:04:08,270
Don't read the description 
straight off the brochure.

191
00:04:08,270 --> 00:04:10,250
The Dragon's Tears?

192
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:13,540
It was something Lord Shadow 
told us on that fateful day.

193
00:04:13,540 --> 00:04:14,980
That fateful day?

194
00:04:19,490 --> 00:04:21,740
Playtime is over.

195
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:25,330
We've finished over here, too.

196
00:04:25,330 --> 00:04:27,400
All cleaned up.

197
00:04:27,810 --> 00:04:30,290
You can't have them...

198
00:04:30,290 --> 00:04:36,170
Y-You'll never have... the Dragon's Tears...

199
00:04:36,170 --> 00:04:38,900
Those golden...

200
00:04:43,310 --> 00:04:44,470
What is the matter, Shadow?

201
00:04:44,470 --> 00:04:46,430
Is something wrong?

202
00:04:45,290 --> 00:04:46,430
Is something...

203
00:04:46,430 --> 00:04:46,920
Oops.

204
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:49,890
Do you know of the Dragon's Tears?

205
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:52,040
I've heard of it.

206
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:55,900
I believe there was a reference 
to something like that in this region's folklore.

207
00:04:57,010 --> 00:05:00,170
A legend that has slumbered since ancient times. 
It is salvation for the soul.

208
00:05:00,170 --> 00:05:02,070
Dig up the entire region.

209
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:03,900
What do you mean?

210
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:05,160
Surely you can see it.

211
00:05:05,850 --> 00:05:09,120
The dazzling radiance that fills the land...

212
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:13,620
The golden tears, 
raining down from the heavens...

213
00:05:14,110 --> 00:05:16,700
Now, dig.

214
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:22,840
Three days later, 
he left the region in a terrible hurry.

215
00:05:23,350 --> 00:05:27,210
Surely he was off on a crucial mission 
that only he was capable of accomplishing.

216
00:05:27,210 --> 00:05:29,000
It's always like that with him.

217
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,980
He goes on ahead, 
leaving the rest of us behind.

218
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:36,210
But if that is his choice, 
we will abide by it.

219
00:05:36,210 --> 00:05:41,210
If he has unfinished business here, 
then we will finish it in his place.

220
00:05:41,210 --> 00:05:43,790
But what could we possibly find here?

221
00:05:43,790 --> 00:05:46,890
Uh, I found something.

222
00:05:50,310 --> 00:05:51,440
Is this...

223
00:05:51,440 --> 00:05:53,580
Yes, a hot spring.

224
00:05:57,610 --> 00:05:59,380
And that's what happened.

225
00:05:59,380 --> 00:06:01,520
Oh, yeah. I remember that.

226
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:04,000
I think you doubled up on too many roles.

227
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:07,640
In the end, all we managed to do 
was build Hot Springs Land.

228
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,420
But surely he had more in mind 
than simply to soak in a hot spring.

229
00:06:11,420 --> 00:06:15,770
Lord Shadow did seem to be interested 
in the legend of the dragon.

230
00:06:15,770 --> 00:06:19,000
But we didn't sense 
any dragon magic in the area.

231
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:22,210
Then, maybe the dragon was a metaphor, 
and it has to do with the Cult?

232
00:06:22,210 --> 00:06:25,200
I believe we've already eliminated 
all Cult activity in the region.

233
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:28,120
With the data we currently have, 
it's impossible to know for sure.

234
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:29,840
That is true.

235
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:32,080
But I'm certain we'll find out more

236
00:06:32,420 --> 00:06:35,090
if we go on this hot springs date with him.

237
00:06:38,460 --> 00:06:41,500
We gave him a total of six tickets.

238
00:06:42,090 --> 00:06:45,960
With his two school friends, 
that brings our lord's party to three.

239
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:48,920
Then, it would be reasonable 
to match him three for three.

240
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:50,130
Three of us...

241
